Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||05-10-2001||10:53 PM||||Hey, im looking at a 86 GT with the 4-spd manual tranny(i belive its 4, not 5, not sure it makes much diffrence)  Anyway, the car starts right up, sounds great reves good, dosent smoke, etc, ect, however, the car wont move at all, any of the forward gears, or reverse, the clutch peadal feels "normal" to me, however i dont ever drive a manual car except on rare ocasions, anyway, as best I can tell it seems normal.  So, my question?  What am I most likely looking at??  Dose it sound like a broken linkage or something worse, like the entire clutch asembly? Or Something else, or what??   Thanks for your help? ||||reg||11
Z||000001||lowCG||05-10-2001||11:46 PM||||So your car won't go into gear?<BR>Guess I don't understand the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MEC91Firebird||05-11-2001||12:06 AM||||I have no idea what the car is doing, The motor runs, and you can move the gear shifter all around, seems to be no binding or force required, but...  the car never wants to go anywhere, regardless of the position of the gear shifter.  So i assume the gears are not even being moved or engaged, no noise coming from it period, so, I assume the tranny is dead, or the linkage has broken, hope this helps, im really intrested in buying the car, needs new paint, or a good polish, but for  $600, cant go wrong! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-11-2001||06:53 AM||||Sounds like a broken shift cable. Two cables opperate the shifter. One, the shift cable, is the front to rear motion of the lever and translates to the turning motion on the transmission. The other, the selector cable, control the gate and translates to the in-out motion at the transmission.  <BR>Open the engine cover and have someone move the shifter through the gears while watching the linkage.<BR>It will likely move in and out but not turn.<BR>You can manually turn to place it in gear to test.||||reg||1
